WEBVTT

00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:14.860
<b>Everything Becomes F: The Perfect Insider</b>

00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:15.070
<b>Everything Becomes F: The Perfect Insider</b>

00:01:36.110 --> 00:01:37.990
<b>Everything Becomes F: The Perfect Insider</b>

00:01:37.990 --> 00:01:43.990
<b>Chapter Three                  Red Magic</b>

00:01:53.310 --> 00:01:54.520
It stinks.

00:01:55.160 --> 00:01:56.520
Of course it does.

00:01:56.520 --> 00:01:58.420
It smells like something rotten.

00:01:59.530 --> 00:02:01.680
Hey, it's pitch-black.

00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:02.670
Is the power out?

00:02:03.260 --> 00:02:05.850
Yuminaga-sensei, get over here!

00:02:05.850 --> 00:02:07.260
Look at this!

00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:08.480
What is this?

00:02:09.180 --> 00:02:10.440
What in the...

00:02:14.690 --> 00:02:16.000
She's dead.

00:02:16.860 --> 00:02:19.780
That's definitely Dr. Magata.

00:02:19.780 --> 00:02:21.490
She's been placed on a P1.

00:02:21.920 --> 00:02:23.850
Is it suicide?

00:02:23.850 --> 00:02:26.980
Like she put on that dress and 
programmed the robot?

00:02:29.920 --> 00:02:33.180
<i>Reset successfully completed.</i>

00:02:33.180 --> 00:02:35.380
We have to call the police now!

00:02:35.380 --> 00:02:38.370
No... It wasn't suicide.

00:02:39.300 --> 00:02:40.610
She was murdered.

00:02:41.620 --> 00:02:43.480
Close that door now.

00:02:46.290 --> 00:02:49.430
Sensei, what are you talking about?

00:02:49.430 --> 00:02:50.940
She was murdered?

00:02:50.940 --> 00:02:53.440
Her arms and legs are missing.

00:02:53.440 --> 00:02:54.830
They've been amputated.

00:02:56.540 --> 00:02:58.140
Who would do that?

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:00.320
The killer.

00:03:00.320 --> 00:03:02.390
And they're inside that room.

00:03:05.580 --> 00:03:10.260
Wait, no one's in that room except Dr. Magata!

00:03:10.260 --> 00:03:11.870
Someone might be in there.

00:03:11.870 --> 00:03:15.250
Otherwise, who could have cut off
 her limbs after she died?

00:03:15.890 --> 00:03:17.000
You're right.

00:03:17.470 --> 00:03:18.960
You're joking...

00:03:18.960 --> 00:03:20.960
Just call the police.

00:03:20.960 --> 00:03:22.220
Do it now.

00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:24.010
Right.

00:03:24.220 --> 00:03:26.700
Are you okay, miss?

00:03:30.260 --> 00:03:33.590
Excuse me. Can I smoke in here?

00:03:33.590 --> 00:03:35.590
Sure, if you like.

00:03:35.590 --> 00:03:37.280
What's going on here?

00:03:37.280 --> 00:03:38.900
The phones aren't working?

00:03:38.900 --> 00:03:40.430
I can't access e-mail, either.

00:03:40.430 --> 00:03:43.280
The entire lab's network has been cut off.

00:03:43.640 --> 00:03:46.240
We can't call the cops like this!

00:03:47.270 --> 00:03:49.120
It's a software issue.

00:03:49.120 --> 00:03:50.230
A problem with Deborah?

00:03:50.230 --> 00:03:52.600
I'm not seeing any problems with the system.

00:03:52.600 --> 00:03:54.750
Part of Deborah must be out of control...

00:03:54.750 --> 00:03:57.410
I refuse to believe she'd randomly 
go out of control now!

00:03:57.410 --> 00:04:00.250
But there's no way for a virus to enter the system.

00:04:00.250 --> 00:04:02.500
That's the only thing I can think of!

00:04:02.500 --> 00:04:05.010
Just keep working!

00:04:15.020 --> 00:04:16.180
Are you okay?

00:04:17.460 --> 00:04:20.720
Nishinosono-kun? Are you okay?

00:04:24.840 --> 00:04:26.500
Now what?

00:04:27.730 --> 00:04:29.880
I may be mistaken,

00:04:29.880 --> 00:04:34.790
but did you just ask me two 
or three times if I was okay?

00:04:35.190 --> 00:04:37.310
Not three times.

00:04:37.780 --> 00:04:40.100
Then you were worried about me.

00:04:40.100 --> 00:04:41.930
Thank you very much.

00:04:44.440 --> 00:04:47.460
I was sure you said it three times, though...

00:04:47.460 --> 00:04:50.430
I did not, and you shouldn't act so happy.

00:04:51.010 --> 00:04:53.700
Whether I'm happy or not is a secret.

00:04:53.700 --> 00:04:57.650
He told you to meet with me, right?

00:04:57.650 --> 00:04:59.130
"He"?

00:04:59.130 --> 00:05:01.440
Saikawa-sensei.

00:05:01.850 --> 00:05:05.030
No... I came here on my own.

00:05:05.030 --> 00:05:07.070
I came because I'm interested in you.

00:05:07.070 --> 00:05:09.850
I lied about wanting to hear about my father.

00:05:10.960 --> 00:05:12.540
You are a very honest girl, aren't you?

00:05:14.540 --> 00:05:17.650
You were raised in a wealthy family.

00:05:17.650 --> 00:05:19.990
Was your father very strict?

00:05:19.990 --> 00:05:22.120
And... Hmm...

00:05:22.120 --> 00:05:25.380
You are attracted to Saikawa-sensei, aren't you?

00:05:26.960 --> 00:05:30.910
Saikawa-sensei was my father's last student.

00:05:30.910 --> 00:05:34.210
A brilliant man, with a very innovative 
method of thinking.

00:05:34.210 --> 00:05:35.150
He is worthy of respect—

00:05:35.150 --> 00:05:36.560
That is not an answer.

00:05:39.620 --> 00:05:41.570
The answer is yes.

00:05:41.570 --> 00:05:45.470
What made you like him so much?

00:05:47.640 --> 00:05:49.570
It was because...

00:05:50.260 --> 00:05:51.570
Why?

00:05:57.400 --> 00:06:00.040
It's been several days since her death.

00:06:00.040 --> 00:06:01.350
Several days?

00:06:01.350 --> 00:06:04.260
We won't know the details until we investigate,

00:06:04.260 --> 00:06:06.090
but should we tell everyone?

00:06:07.990 --> 00:06:10.210
No need.

00:06:10.210 --> 00:06:14.110
It isn't like telling them will change anything.

00:06:14.110 --> 00:06:18.080
And if we stay here and keep an 
eye out, the killer can't escape.

00:06:18.080 --> 00:06:19.520
That won't work.

00:06:20.400 --> 00:06:22.600
No one's in that room.

00:06:22.600 --> 00:06:23.610
We guarantee it.

00:06:24.030 --> 00:06:27.540
If no one's there, then how 
did she end up like that?

00:06:27.540 --> 00:06:28.700
Absolutely no one's there.

00:06:28.700 --> 00:06:30.910
Then has the killer already escaped?

00:06:30.910 --> 00:06:32.900
No one went in or out.

00:06:32.900 --> 00:06:34.650
We've been here the whole time,

00:06:34.650 --> 00:06:36.180
and we checked the video logs, too.

00:06:36.180 --> 00:06:37.120
Video logs?

00:06:37.120 --> 00:06:39.500
Then who killed her?

00:06:39.500 --> 00:06:41.090
You tell me.

00:06:41.090 --> 00:06:42.750
And don't say it was a ghost.

00:06:42.750 --> 00:06:45.660
Hey, look at me and say that again!

00:06:45.660 --> 00:06:47.960
Okay, just calm down.

00:06:48.820 --> 00:06:49.960
Um...

00:06:52.620 --> 00:06:56.420
Couldn't we find out instantly by looking inside?

00:06:56.420 --> 00:06:58.100
It's too dangerous.

00:06:58.100 --> 00:07:00.550
There's a murderer inside.

00:07:00.550 --> 00:07:02.300
I told you there isn't!

00:07:02.300 --> 00:07:04.250
If you want, I'll go in there alone!

00:07:04.250 --> 00:07:07.150
Let's just leave him locked in, 
and wait for the cops.

00:07:07.150 --> 00:07:09.650
There are no other entrances or exits, right?

00:07:09.650 --> 00:07:13.930
No, there's no other way in and or out.

00:07:15.260 --> 00:07:17.190
Only one entrance?

00:07:18.370 --> 00:07:20.160
Once the cops get here,

00:07:20.740 --> 00:07:23.000
they'll suspect all of us, right?

00:07:25.780 --> 00:07:26.760
That's right.

00:07:26.760 --> 00:07:28.270
That's right!

00:07:28.270 --> 00:07:30.270
First, we should wait for the director.

00:07:30.270 --> 00:07:31.410
The director, huh?

00:07:31.410 --> 00:07:33.410
He's coming here by helicopter.

00:07:33.410 --> 00:07:36.740
Once he returns, we can use the helicopter's 
radio to contact the outside.

00:07:36.740 --> 00:07:39.350
Right now, it's our only choice!

00:07:39.350 --> 00:07:41.630
When is he coming back?

00:07:41.630 --> 00:07:44.710
The plan was that he'd be back 
in about thirty minutes...

00:07:46.510 --> 00:07:49.360
Dr. Magata's younger sister is with him.

00:07:50.790 --> 00:07:57.060
Her sister will be very sad 
when she hears what happened.

00:07:59.180 --> 00:08:00.560
Saikawa-sensei...

00:08:01.380 --> 00:08:02.930
I'm sorry.

00:08:02.930 --> 00:08:05.580
You got caught up in this because of me.

00:08:06.660 --> 00:08:09.380
It's because you're a rain girl.

00:08:10.260 --> 00:08:11.790
What do you mean?

00:08:12.130 --> 00:08:13.940
It's a joke...

00:08:14.310 --> 00:08:15.400
No meaning.

00:08:15.720 --> 00:08:18.510
Which means you're a clear-skies man, doesn't it?

00:08:18.510 --> 00:08:20.640
And I'm a rain girl.

00:08:21.100 --> 00:08:23.640
That's why I always have an umbrella.

00:08:24.160 --> 00:08:27.150
No umbrella can ward off murder.

00:08:27.550 --> 00:08:31.080
Is there an umbrella that can keep away death?

00:08:40.700 --> 00:08:43.040
I wonder how I can laugh right now.

00:08:43.540 --> 00:08:45.990
You seem to be laughing at me.

00:08:45.990 --> 00:08:48.290
I most certainly am not.

00:08:52.300 --> 00:08:53.760
It's strange.

00:08:54.160 --> 00:08:55.800
Indeed, it is.

00:08:56.430 --> 00:08:59.710
After what happened to Dr. Magata, 
I can't believe I can laugh.

00:09:00.600 --> 00:09:03.790
I may have reached
 an emotional peak and shut down.

00:09:04.380 --> 00:09:08.770
If nothing else, I did manage to 
meet Dr. Magata in person.

00:09:09.220 --> 00:09:11.880
Did you see where the body was amputated?

00:09:15.690 --> 00:09:17.190
I wish I hadn't.

00:09:17.190 --> 00:09:18.130
Wow.

00:09:18.130 --> 00:09:19.540
It doesn't bother you, does it?

00:09:19.540 --> 00:09:22.880
My blood pressure's low to begin 
with, so it balanced out.

00:09:23.270 --> 00:09:28.080
Her arms and legs are inside that room, 
if the killer didn't take them.

00:09:28.520 --> 00:09:30.080
And why did he amputate them?

00:09:30.080 --> 00:09:32.090
To put that bridal gown on her.

00:09:32.450 --> 00:09:33.460
It can't be.

00:09:48.150 --> 00:09:52.690
What's this "Red Magic" thing I keep seeing?

00:09:52.690 --> 00:09:54.940
This isn't UNIX?

00:09:55.350 --> 00:09:59.200
That's what we call our custom, in-house system.

00:09:59.200 --> 00:10:01.270
It's currently on version four,

00:10:01.270 --> 00:10:03.950
and the development environment 
is extremely feature-rich.

00:10:04.460 --> 00:10:06.960
Once you experience it, you'll never 
be able to work anywhere else.

00:10:06.960 --> 00:10:08.710
Is it that amazing?

00:10:09.030 --> 00:10:10.460
It's that amazing.

00:10:10.460 --> 00:10:13.090
But the network was still cut off?

00:10:14.740 --> 00:10:17.340
You don't mind hitting where it hurts, do you?

00:10:17.650 --> 00:10:19.190
It's so strange.

00:10:19.760 --> 00:10:23.660
Like Deborah says, there was an unexpected error.

00:10:23.960 --> 00:10:25.140
With Red Magic.

00:10:25.990 --> 00:10:27.640
<i>Red Magic...</i>

00:10:28.500 --> 00:10:31.110
<i>Red refers to a color.</i>

00:10:31.530 --> 00:10:32.860
<i>Communism.</i>

00:10:33.310 --> 00:10:35.520
<i>And blood.</i>

00:10:37.680 --> 00:10:39.680
<i>Dr. Magata Shiki's room</i>

00:10:40.270 --> 00:10:42.090
<i>has only one entrance.</i>

00:11:02.140 --> 00:11:03.920
Saikawa-sensei!

00:11:05.240 --> 00:11:08.560
How can you look so excited?

00:11:08.560 --> 00:11:11.350
Because you've figured something out, haven't you?

00:11:11.350 --> 00:11:13.370
I know you have.

00:11:14.350 --> 00:11:15.820
That's what my face says to you?

00:11:16.350 --> 00:11:19.280
I don't think that expression is 
in my repertoire, though.

00:11:19.720 --> 00:11:21.570
Not your face. Your cigarette.

00:11:21.570 --> 00:11:23.800
It proves you were thinking about something.

00:11:25.460 --> 00:11:26.910
Very logical.

00:11:27.520 --> 00:11:29.080
Come on, tell me!

00:11:30.200 --> 00:11:33.080
When Dr. Magata Shiki's body appeared,

00:11:33.080 --> 00:11:35.200
that door was open.

00:11:35.670 --> 00:11:37.430
It was very noisy,

00:11:37.430 --> 00:11:40.260
and we all focused on the doctor's body.

00:11:41.050 --> 00:11:43.400
During that time, it would've been possible

00:11:43.400 --> 00:11:46.350
to escape the room and board the elevator.

00:11:46.610 --> 00:11:48.450
Too bad, Sensei.

00:11:50.000 --> 00:11:51.850
Is that all you've got?

00:11:51.850 --> 00:11:56.030
Your expression says you disagree 
with something I said.

00:11:57.060 --> 00:12:00.420
Sensei, it would have been impossible.

00:12:03.120 --> 00:12:05.630
May we come bother you again?

00:12:05.630 --> 00:12:07.620
Sure, as often as you want.

00:12:09.000 --> 00:12:12.130
This is the room where they monitor Dr. Magata.

00:12:12.130 --> 00:12:15.800
Yeah, but it's not that big a deal.

00:12:15.800 --> 00:12:19.130
We just check what goes into her room.

00:12:19.130 --> 00:12:22.050
Big things go through that yellow door.

00:12:22.050 --> 00:12:24.660
And small things go through the mail slot.

00:12:24.660 --> 00:12:26.990
Oh, I forgot to ask.

00:12:26.990 --> 00:12:29.390
How big an object can fit through there?

00:12:29.390 --> 00:12:33.720
250 mm x 250 mm x 350 mm.

00:12:33.720 --> 00:12:37.160
21,875 cc, huh?

00:12:37.580 --> 00:12:39.400
A person couldn't fit through that.

00:12:39.400 --> 00:12:41.620
Did you just do the math?

00:12:41.920 --> 00:12:45.380
Did you bring any large objects through that door?

00:12:45.380 --> 00:12:47.120
Big enough for a person to fit inside?

00:12:47.120 --> 00:12:50.580
A little while ago, she got a new microwave.

00:12:51.160 --> 00:12:53.470
Naturally, we looked inside.

00:12:53.970 --> 00:12:55.600
What's amazing is that

00:12:55.600 --> 00:12:59.420
they have complete video records 
for the past fifteen years.

00:12:59.760 --> 00:13:02.600
Video records for fifteen years?

00:13:03.800 --> 00:13:05.850
This video shows that

00:13:05.850 --> 00:13:09.430
Dr. Magata hasn't left her room in fifteen years.

00:13:09.750 --> 00:13:12.260
Of course, that isn't restricted to her.

00:13:12.260 --> 00:13:14.110
No one else entered.

00:13:14.550 --> 00:13:16.870
For fifteen years, huh?

00:13:18.790 --> 00:13:19.800
Ah, wait!

00:13:36.180 --> 00:13:38.580
I've been wondering...

00:13:38.580 --> 00:13:41.340
What's this? Do you play music?

00:13:41.600 --> 00:13:42.630
A marimba.

00:13:43.580 --> 00:13:45.110
Wow!

00:13:45.110 --> 00:13:46.220
Want to try it?

00:13:46.870 --> 00:13:47.840
No, thanks.

00:13:49.840 --> 00:13:52.430
Sensei, wait!

00:14:01.150 --> 00:14:04.700
I think it has something to do with 
what happened fifteen years ago.

00:14:05.090 --> 00:14:09.170
I mean, now three people from 
the Magata family have died.

00:14:09.170 --> 00:14:10.480
Further,

00:14:10.480 --> 00:14:14.620
remember who Director Shindo's bringing back?

00:14:15.300 --> 00:14:17.620
Dr. Magata Shiki's younger sister.

00:14:18.060 --> 00:14:19.510
Yes, that's right.

00:14:20.310 --> 00:14:22.150
Now, of all times,

00:14:22.150 --> 00:14:25.030
the Magata family's surviving member shows up.

00:14:25.030 --> 00:14:26.470
A little too perfect, don't you think?

00:14:27.120 --> 00:14:28.870
I'm afraid I don't know

00:14:28.870 --> 00:14:31.640
the definition of "a little too perfect."

00:14:31.640 --> 00:14:33.890
Let's forget about definitions here.

00:14:34.390 --> 00:14:38.020
You're trying to say the killer's after 
the Magata fortune or something?

00:14:38.430 --> 00:14:39.770
That's what it means.

00:14:39.770 --> 00:14:42.870
Then I don't think it would be necessary

00:14:42.870 --> 00:14:45.930
to amputate her limbs and put 
her in a wedding dress.

00:14:46.960 --> 00:14:48.280
That's true.

00:14:50.080 --> 00:14:52.010
That's true, isn't it?

00:14:53.280 --> 00:14:56.120
For fifteen years, no one went into the room.

00:14:56.120 --> 00:14:58.790
The only person inside was Dr. Magata.

00:14:59.470 --> 00:15:02.830
How did the killer get inside?

00:15:02.830 --> 00:15:05.670
You don't need to say what you're thinking aloud.

00:15:06.040 --> 00:15:08.500
They do it all the time in mysteries.

00:15:08.500 --> 00:15:10.030
I've always wanted to try it.

00:15:10.330 --> 00:15:12.410
Expository dialogue, right?

00:15:12.890 --> 00:15:14.300
I don't like it.

00:15:15.400 --> 00:15:17.740
Next is the wedding dress.

00:15:18.040 --> 00:15:20.940
I'm sure there must be some meaning to it.

00:15:20.940 --> 00:15:22.200
I'm sure of it.

00:15:23.310 --> 00:15:26.860
Is my definition of the word "sure" all right?

00:15:28.050 --> 00:15:29.150
The director is arriving.

00:15:36.830 --> 00:15:38.210
Yamane Yukihiro.

00:15:43.000 --> 00:15:44.080
Director!

00:15:45.750 --> 00:15:48.130
Use your radio to contact the police!

00:15:48.420 --> 00:15:50.430
Dr. Magata's been killed!

00:15:50.880 --> 00:15:52.820
We don't know who did it.

00:15:52.820 --> 00:15:54.720
The doctor's room was locked.

00:15:54.720 --> 00:15:56.850
The killer may still be inside.

00:15:56.850 --> 00:15:58.510
We can't use e-mail.

00:15:58.510 --> 00:16:00.320
Contact the police now!

00:16:11.260 --> 00:16:12.240
Let's go.

00:16:17.690 --> 00:16:19.990
Director, it's Nishinosono.

00:16:20.290 --> 00:16:23.250
Please tell them I'm in the lab.

00:16:23.250 --> 00:16:25.500
Use my name, and they'll know who I am!

00:16:25.840 --> 00:16:28.320
My uncle is the head of the prefectural police!

00:16:29.380 --> 00:16:31.380
Come here, Nishinosono-san!

00:16:34.550 --> 00:16:35.650
Ma'am...

00:16:36.350 --> 00:16:37.280
Where's my husband?

00:16:37.280 --> 00:16:38.830
He's still on the roof.

00:16:39.340 --> 00:16:42.130
This is Magata Miki-san. 
Could you look after her?

00:16:42.130 --> 00:16:44.150
I'll give you the details later.

00:16:44.150 --> 00:16:48.020
What's happened with Shiki-san 
is simply unbelievable...

00:16:53.990 --> 00:16:55.980
That's her younger sister?

00:16:55.980 --> 00:16:57.230
Miki-san.

00:16:57.530 --> 00:17:00.460
She looks more grown-up than 
Dr. Magata, doesn't she?

00:17:02.380 --> 00:17:06.480
But Dr. Magata stayed in her room for fifteen years.

00:17:06.480 --> 00:17:08.750
She may have looked younger than she really was.

00:17:10.330 --> 00:17:13.210
But they really do look alike...

00:17:14.470 --> 00:17:19.390
I said that, after meeting Dr. Magata in person, 
I'd reached an emotional peak, but...
